      "writtenOn": "2026-10-21T00:07:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If a future convertible requires CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_POWER_BUTTON_KEYBOARD, but doesn\u0027t have the display backlight gpio, then the power button as a wake source would still fail. Should this be a required DT node?\n\nWe could either:\n  1. Use a Devicetree binding YAML with \"required: true\" for the GPIO property (which aligns well with how we         \n  configure modern Zephyr features and catches missing properties at CMake time).\n  2. Add a BUILD_ASSERT(DT_NODE_EXISTS(DT_ALIAS(gpio_pb_suppress_en))) when  CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_POWER_BUTTON_KEYBOARD  \n  is defined, which prevents compilation if the alias is missing and lets us drop the runtime #if guards. \n  \nI think option #1 is more inline with what we\u0027ve been doing in zephyr.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 482,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 482,
        "endChar": 49
      },
      "revId": "7804af9ccdbb6b4044f961d1519e760706cb5839",
